WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
In his youth, Duke Wen of Jin lived in exile abroad for many years.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.638
He traveled through many states and endured much hardship.

00:00:06.988 --> 00:00:10.108
The men who followed him remained utterly loyal to him.

00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:13.218
The state of Chu once received him warmly and helped him.

00:00:13.568 --> 00:00:16.808
Duke Wen was deeply grateful, and made a promise.

00:00:17.158 --> 00:00:20.086
The King of Chu treated him as an honored guest and gave him many gifts.

00:00:20.436 --> 00:00:23.724
He said: if our two states ever go to war, the Jin army will first retreat three she.

00:00:24.074 --> 00:00:27.002
One she is about thirty li, so three she is ninety li.

00:00:27.352 --> 00:00:30.520
Everyone present silently admired his answer.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.558
Many years later, Jin and Chu truly met in the field.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:37.388
Duke Wen remembered his promise of those years, and ordered the retreat.

00:00:37.738 --> 00:00:40.426
The soldiers of both armies watched each other tensely.

00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:43.824
The Jin army retreated in good order for ninety li before stopping.

00:00:44.174 --> 00:00:47.582
The Chu army pursued all the way, slowly growing proud and careless.

00:00:47.932 --> 00:00:51.292
This retreat let the Jin army avoid the Chu army's sharpest edge.

00:00:51.642 --> 00:00:55.194
Retreating three she was not only keeping faith — it was also good strategy.

00:00:55.544 --> 00:00:58.592
Later people used this idiom to mean making a willing concession.

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:01.630
The man who kept his word in the end won everyone's trust.

